# Quiets the podman-docker shim (2026-09-06). /usr/bin/docker, the script
# podman-docker installs, checks for this file and /etc/containers/nodocker
# before writing "Emulate Docker CLI using podman." to stderr on EVERY
# invocation. Without it, anything that pipes, greps or fails a build on
# docker's stderr sees output a real Docker would never produce — which is
# the one thing the shim exists to avoid.
#
# Only existence is tested, never content, so this comment is free. The
# per-user path is deliberate over the /etc one: it needs no root, so a
# plain `chezmoi apply` lands it on every machine with nothing to authorize.
